  "interpretation": [
    "World AABB removes about 78.8% of mesh queries, but leaves mesh node visits and triangle tests unchanged; the skipped calls were predominantly cheap mesh-root rejections.",
    "World AABB adds 2685680 outer bounds tests. Its combined outer/mesh bounds count exceeds the original mesh bounds count despite fewer mesh queries.",
    "The scene BVH reduces triangle tests by only about 3.75% and mesh node visits by 2.46%, while adding 1937780 top-level node entries and 2705617 bounds tests. Sixteen material-group meshes with large overlapping extents provide limited object-level pruning.",
    "The TLAS kernel also has a larger reported stack frame. These observations are consistent with the slowdown, but do not isolate hardware-level causes.",
    "The AABB median differs from the preserved executable by less than 0.1% and is slightly slower than the candidate-disabled median, with overlapping ranges. It is not a demonstrated speedup."
  ],
